From fc794ec1658b463f3411a85593545eb6df1e9e15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 21:28:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] first boot: enforce the credential and Wi-Fi gate in httpd,
 not only in JS

The first-boot wizard kept being reported as not working. Two structural holes,
not a logic slip.

The Wi-Fi step was never reached. The credential step ended by navigating to
Main_ReaperDash.asp, and the dashboard deliberately does not load state.js - it
carries its own credential guard instead - while the Wi-Fi gate lived only in
state.js. So the moment credentials were set the box landed on the one page
where that gate could not run, and went into the GUI on the factory Wi-Fi
password.

And the gate was bypassable. Enforcement was entirely client-side, but only 128
of the 245 .asp pages carry a state.js include, so typing the URL of any of the
other 117 walked straight past the wizard.

Enforcement therefore moves to the only chokepoint that sees every request.
reaper_firstboot_pending() / reaper_firstboot_allowed() in httpd.c bounce any
.asp or .htm load to the wizard while first boot is incomplete - page loads
only, so CGIs, assets and the update_* pollers are untouched, and the cheap
string tests run before any nvram read. The allow-list keeps login, device
discovery, the framed wireless page and AiMesh onboarding working.

The wizard now owns both steps: it leaves only when credentials and Wi-Fi are
both done, and step 2 activates the previously-dead progress bar and frames the
stock wireless page inside the Reaper card. That framing is deliberate - this
model is MULTILAN_MWL, so the main Wi-Fi is SDN-driven, and a hand-rolled PSK
write is exactly how a setting ships that looks saved and is not. The wizard
owns the chrome and the exit; the apply stays the proven path. state.js's two
wireless gates now target the wizard, so there is one surface and one place
that decides first boot is finished.

Lockout safety, because this gate can strand a user in their own router: it
fires only from live state, so a configured or upgraded box never sees it; the
Wi-Fi condition applies to router and AP modes only, because a repeater or
media bridge legitimately leaves w_Setting at 0; and reaper_fbdone=1 is an
unconditional escape hatch honoured by the C gate, state.js and the dashboard
guard alike. It is deliberately not written by the wizard - the gate opens on
its own when the live conditions clear, so there is no new write path to fail.

Verified without a build: a state-machine simulator models all four redirect
layers and walks each scenario to a fixed point, failing on any cycle - the
historical failure mode here. 24/24 across factory reset, credentials-set,
both-done, upgraded box, escape hatch, repeater mode, theme kill-switch and
operator-forced change, with no loops. It caught two real defects in the first
cut: state.js ignored the escape hatch, and the repeater exclusion was missing
from the dashboard guard and the wizard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/httpd/httpd.c            | 102 ++++++++++++++++++++
 release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp  |  14 ++-
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp |  71 +++++++++++++-
 release/src/router/www/state.js             |  29 ++++--
 4 files changed, 206 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/httpd/httpd.c b/release/src/router/httpd/httpd.c
index 5cd032e662..57968aa5de 100644
--- a/release/src/router/httpd/httpd.c
+++ b/release/src/router/httpd/httpd.c
@@ -1292,6 +1292,92 @@ gk_mac_known(const char *mac)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* ===================================================================
+ * reaper 2026-08-11: SERVER-SIDE first-boot / factory-reset gate.
+ *
+ * Until this build, first-boot enforcement was entirely client-side: state.js
+ * redirects plus per-page <head> guards. That leaks badly - only 128 of the 245
+ * .asp pages carry a state.js <script src> at all, so typing the URL of any of
+ * the other 117 walked straight past the wizard. Worse, the credential step ended
+ * by sending the browser to Main_ReaperDash.asp, which deliberately does NOT load
+ * state.js (it carries its own credential guard instead) - so the Wi-Fi step that
+ * state.js is supposed to force was simply never reached. That is why a box could
+ * come up on a factory Wi-Fi password with the admin credentials already changed,
+ * and why this kept being reported as "still not working".
+ *
+ * Enforcement therefore moves to where it cannot be routed around. The GUI is a
+ * static page set - the only chokepoint that sees every request is httpd itself.
+ *
+ * SAFETY (this gate can lock a user out of their own router if it misfires):
+ *   - it only ever fires while the box is genuinely unconfigured, from LIVE state
+ *     (default admin password, operator-forced change, or wireless never set up);
+ *     an upgraded box that is already configured never sees it;
+ *   - it applies ONLY to .asp/.htm page loads - never to CGIs, assets, or the
+ *     polling endpoints, so the wizard, login and AiMesh onboarding keep working;
+ *   - `reaper_fbdone=1` is an unconditional escape hatch: an operator who somehow
+ *     gets stuck can clear the gate over SSH with
+ *       nvram set reaper_fbdone=1 && nvram commit
+ *     It is deliberately NOT written by the wizard - the gate opens on its own when
+ *     the live conditions clear, so there is no new write path to get wrong. */
+static int
+reaper_firstboot_pending(void)
+{
+	const char *ri = nvram_get("reaper_inject");
+
+	/* Reaper UI killed -> stock owns first boot; do not interfere. */
+	if (ri && *ri && atoi(ri) == 0)
+		return 0;
+	/* operator escape hatch */
+	if (nvram_match("reaper_fbdone", "1"))
+		return 0;
+	if (!check_if_file_exist("/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp"))
+		return 0;
+	if (nvram_get_int("force_chgpass"))
+		return 1;
+	if (is_passwd_default())
+		return 1;
+	/* Wireless never configured. w_Setting is stock's own "wireless has been set up"
+	 * flag - factory default 0 (restored to stock by the AiMesh-node fix), auto-set
+	 * to 1 by the stock wireless apply. Using stock's flag rather than a Reaper one
+	 * means the gate opens through the PROVEN apply path: this box is MULTILAN_MWL,
+	 * where the main Wi-Fi is SDN-driven, so a hand-rolled PSK write would be exactly
+	 * the kind of change that silently does not stick.
+	 *
+	 * Router and AP modes only (sw_mode 1 / 3), mirroring state.js's own wireless
+	 * gate. A repeater or media bridge does not run its own wireless config, so
+	 * w_Setting legitimately stays 0 there - gating on it would wedge those boxes out
+	 * of their GUI permanently, which is exactly the failure this must not cause. */
+	{
+		int sw = nvram_get_int("sw_mode");
+		if ((sw == 1 || sw == 3) && nvram_match("w_Setting", "0"))
+			return 1;
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* Pages that must stay reachable while the gate is closed. Substring match: the
+ * wizard itself, the login/logout surfaces it bounces through, device discovery,
+ * the stock wireless page (the wizard FRAMES it for its Wi-Fi step, so it must
+ * load), and the QIS/onboarding pages AiMesh runs framed. */
+static int
+reaper_firstboot_allowed(const char *u)
+{
+	static const char *allow[] = {
+		"Reaper_FirstBoot.asp",
+		"Main_Login.asp", "Logout.asp", "Nologin.asp",
+		"find_device.asp",
+		"Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp",
+		"QIS_", "amas", "cfg_onboarding",
+		NULL
+	};
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; allow[i]; i++)
+		if (strstr(u, allow[i]))
+			return 1;
+	return 0;
+}
+
 int
 reaper_gk_captive_check(const char *client_ip)
 {
@@ -1652,6 +1738,22 @@ handle_request(void)
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* reaper 2026-08-11: first-boot gate (see reaper_firstboot_pending above). Page
+	 * loads only - CGIs, assets and the update_* pollers are untouched - and the
+	 * cheap string tests run before any nvram read. top.location so it also escapes
+	 * the shell frame rather than drawing the wizard inside it. */
+	if ((strstr(url, ".asp") || strstr(url, ".htm"))
+	    && !strstr(url, "update_networkmapd.asp")
+	    && !strstr(url, "update_clients.asp")
+	    && !strstr(url, "update_customList.asp")
+	    && !reaper_firstboot_allowed(url)
+	    && reaper_firstboot_pending()) {
+		send_page(200, "OK", (char *)0,
+			"<meta charset=\"utf-8\">"
+			"<script>top.location.replace('/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp');</script>", 0);
+		return;
+	}
+
 #if !defined(RTCONFIG_HND_ROUTER)
 	if (!strncmp(file, "Main_Login.asp", 14) && (uptime() - flush_cache_t1) > 10 * 60) {
 		/* free pagecahe when login, don't do it again in 10 minutes. */
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp b/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
index 58220e3fc5..688f8de5f6 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
@@ -14,7 +14,19 @@
    Runs during head parse (location.replace) so a default-cred box never renders. */
 (function(){
   var pwdef = '<% check_pw(); %>', force = '<% nvram_get("force_chgpass"); %>';
-  if((pwdef == 1 || force == 1) && location.pathname.toUpperCase().indexOf('REAPER_FIRSTBOOT') < 0)
+  /* v2.3.5: ALSO gate on the Wi-Fi step. This page is the wizard's exit target, and
+     because it does not load state.js it was the hole through which a box reached the
+     UI with its credentials changed but the factory Wi-Fi password intact - the Wi-Fi
+     gate lives in state.js and simply never ran here. reaper_fbdone is the operator
+     escape hatch (see reaper_firstboot_pending() in httpd/httpd.c). */
+  var wifidef = '<% nvram_get("w_Setting"); %>', esc = '<% nvram_get("reaper_fbdone"); %>';
+  /* Router (1) and AP (3) only: a repeater or media bridge runs no wireless config of
+     its own, so w_Setting legitimately stays 0 there and gating on it would wedge
+     those boxes out of the GUI. Mirrors state.js and reaper_firstboot_pending(). */
+  var swm = parseInt('<% nvram_get("sw_mode"); %>', 10);
+  var wifiGate = (wifidef == 0 && (swm == 1 || swm == 3));
+  if(esc != 1 && (pwdef == 1 || force == 1 || wifiGate)
+     && location.pathname.toUpperCase().indexOf('REAPER_FIRSTBOOT') < 0)
     location.replace('Reaper_FirstBoot.asp?nextPage=Main_ReaperDash.asp');
 })();
 </script>
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp
index 60987c79b9..9491d64cd1 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp
@@ -137,6 +137,21 @@ input:focus{border-color:var(--crimson)}
      response never reached the page. Leave instead of dead-ending. */
   var RFB_PW_IS_DEFAULT=('<% check_pw(); %>'==='1');
   var RFB_FORCE_CHG=('<% nvram_get("force_chgpass"); %>'==='1');
+  /* v2.3.5: the wizard now owns BOTH first-boot steps. Step 2 (Wi-Fi) used to be
+     handed off to the stock wireless page by a state.js redirect - but the
+     credential step finished by navigating to Main_ReaperDash.asp, which does not
+     load state.js, so the hand-off never happened and the Wi-Fi step was skipped
+     outright. Step 2 is now driven from HERE, with the proven stock wireless page
+     framed inside this card: one Reaper surface end to end, and the Wi-Fi apply is
+     still the stock SDN/MWL path rather than a hand-rolled PSK write. */
+  /* Router (1) and AP (3) only - a repeater / media bridge runs no wireless config of
+     its own, so w_Setting legitimately stays 0 there and step 2 must not be demanded
+     (it would strand those boxes in the wizard). Mirrors state.js and
+     reaper_firstboot_pending() in httpd/httpd.c. */
+  var RFB_SWM=parseInt('<% nvram_get("sw_mode"); %>',10);
+  var RFB_WIFI_PENDING=('<% nvram_get("w_Setting"); %>'==='0' && (RFB_SWM===1||RFB_SWM===3));
+  var RFB_ESCAPE=('<% nvram_get("reaper_fbdone"); %>'==='1');
+  var RFB_CRED_PENDING=(RFB_PW_IS_DEFAULT||RFB_FORCE_CHG);
   /* v2.2.0 (field: v2.1.6 first-boot refresh-loop): leave to the DASHBOARD, never to
      "/". httpd's startup-cached indexpage could still say THIS page after the
      credential step (that flow never restarts httpd), so leaving to "/" re-served the
@@ -145,7 +160,9 @@ input:focus{border-color:var(--crimson)}
      this target is structurally loop-proof; with a dead session it lands on the login
      page with the dashboard as the stored next page - the correct flow. The cache
      itself is also fixed (live recompute in httpd.c / web.c login_cgi). */
-  if(!RFB_PW_IS_DEFAULT && !RFB_FORCE_CHG){ location.replace("/Main_ReaperDash.asp"); }
+  /* Leave ONLY when both steps are genuinely done (or the operator escape hatch is
+     set). Bouncing out on "credentials done" alone is what skipped the Wi-Fi step. */
+  if(RFB_ESCAPE || (!RFB_CRED_PENDING && !RFB_WIFI_PENDING)){ location.replace("/Main_ReaperDash.asp"); }
   var DEFAULT_PW = "admin";  /* mirrors defaults.c http_passwd default */
   function $(id){return document.getElementById(id);}
   function showErr(m){var e=$("fb_err"); e.textContent=m; e.style.display="block";}
@@ -239,6 +256,47 @@ input:focus{border-color:var(--crimson)}
     finishOk();
   }
 
+  /* ---- STEP 2: Wi-Fi password -------------------------------------------------
+     Swap the card over to the stock wireless page, framed. Why framed rather than
+     re-implemented: this model is MULTILAN_MWL, so the main Wi-Fi is SDN-driven and
+     the real apply walks sdn_rl / per-band profiles. Re-creating that here is the
+     classic way to ship a setting that appears to save and silently does not - so
+     the wizard drives the PROVEN page and just owns the chrome and the exit.
+     The gate in httpd.c allow-lists Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp precisely so this
+     frame can load; state.js's own wireless gates self-exempt that page, so the
+     frame cannot redirect itself. */
+  function showWifiStep(){
+    try{
+      var card=document.querySelector(".card");
+      if(!card) return;
+      var s2=$("step2bar"); if(s2) s2.className="on";
+      var f=$("fbForm"); if(f) f.style.display="none";
+      var h=card.querySelector("h2"); if(h) h.textContent=`<#RFB_15#>`;
+      var l=card.querySelector(".lead"); if(l) l.textContent=`<#RFB_16#>`;
+      card.style.maxWidth="920px";
+      var fr=document.createElement("iframe");
+      fr.id="fb_wifi";
+      fr.src="/Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp?firstboot=1";
+      fr.setAttribute("title", `<#RFB_15#>`);
+      fr.style.cssText="width:100%;height:70vh;min-height:460px;border:1px solid var(--line-soft);"
+                     + "border-radius:10px;background:#0b0b0e;margin-top:14px";
+      card.appendChild(fr);
+      /* The wireless apply restarts the radios and flips w_Setting to 1. Poll for
+         that rather than guessing at a timeout, then leave to the dashboard. */
+      var tries=0;
+      var iv=setInterval(function(){
+        tries++;
+        var done=false;
+        try{
+          var nv=httpApi.nvramGet(["w_Setting"], true);
+          done=(nv && String(nv.w_Setting)==="1");
+        }catch(e){}
+        if(done){ clearInterval(iv); top.location.href="/Main_ReaperDash.asp"; }
+        else if(tries>900){ clearInterval(iv); }   /* ~30 min; user is still working */
+      }, 2000);
+    }catch(e){}
+  }
+
   function finishOk(){
     try{
       var tf=$("titleForm");
@@ -254,10 +312,19 @@ input:focus{border-color:var(--crimson)}
        dashboard as the stored next page. state.js still forces the Wi-Fi step on the
        stock pages until a PSK is set. Wait a beat longer than stock (3000ms) so the
        apply/commit lands before we leave. */
-    setTimeout(function(){ top.location.href = "/Main_ReaperDash.asp"; }, 3200);
+    setTimeout(function(){
+      /* v2.3.5: continue to the Wi-Fi step instead of leaving. Going straight to the
+         dashboard here is precisely what skipped step 2 - the dashboard does not load
+         state.js, so nothing downstream ever forced the Wi-Fi password. */
+      if(RFB_WIFI_PENDING){ showWifiStep(); return; }
+      top.location.href = "/Main_ReaperDash.asp";
+    }, 3200);
   }
 
   document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function(){
+    /* Credentials already set but Wi-Fi still factory (the httpd gate sent us here,
+       or the user reloaded mid-wizard) -> open straight on step 2. */
+    if(!RFB_ESCAPE && !RFB_CRED_PENDING && RFB_WIFI_PENDING){ showWifiStep(); return; }
     $("fb_go").addEventListener("click", submit);
     $("fbForm").addEventListener("submit", function(e){ e.preventDefault(); submit(); });
     $("fb_pw").addEventListener("keyup", function(e){ if(e.keyCode===13) $("fb_pw2").focus(); });
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/state.js b/release/src/router/www/state.js
index efef034f5d..b25fc1bde6 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/state.js
+++ b/release/src/router/www/state.js
@@ -930,22 +930,37 @@ if(navigator.userAgent.search("asusrouter") == -1){
 	// proven stock wireless page, before any other page is reachable. Derived purely
 	// from live state (default password / unconfigured sdn_rl) so a already-configured
 	// box -- including one upgrading to this build -- never sees the gate.
-	if((notice_pw_is_default == 1 || force_chgpass == 1) && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("QIS_") < 0) //force to change http_passwd / http_username & except QIS settings
+	// reaper v2.3.5: honour the reaper_fbdone escape hatch here too. Without it the C
+	// gate could be cleared over SSH while this gate still bounced every page back to
+	// the wizard - i.e. the hatch would not actually free a wedged GUI. Setting it
+	// requires root on the box already, so it weakens nothing that root cannot do.
+	if(`<% nvram_get("reaper_fbdone"); %>` != '1' && (notice_pw_is_default == 1 || force_chgpass == 1) && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("QIS_") < 0) //force to change http_passwd / http_username & except QIS settings
 		location.href = 'Reaper_FirstBoot.asp?nextPage=' + window.location.pathname.substring(1 ,window.location.pathname.length);
 	// reaper: w_Setting factory default is back to stock 0 (AiMesh node discoverability +
 	// WPS-OOB enrollment - see defaults.c). Stock sent w_Setting==0 boxes to the retired
 	// QIS wireless mini-wizard; route it to the same first-run wireless page as gate 3
 	// instead (target is in reaper_inject.c reaper_skip[] - standing rule 27). Exempt the
 	// target page itself and the QIS wizard (AiMesh add-node runs it framed).
-	else if(`<% nvram_get("w_Setting"); %>` == '0' && !isSwMode("RP") && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("QIS_") < 0 && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("ADVANCED_WIRELESS_CONTENT") < 0)
-		top.location.href = '/Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp?firstboot=1';
+	// reaper v2.3.5: both wireless gates now target the Reaper wizard, not the stock
+	// wireless page directly. The wizard FRAMES that page for its step 2, so the apply
+	// is still the proven SDN/MWL path - but the user only ever sees one Reaper surface,
+	// and there is a single place that decides when first boot is finished. The frame
+	// itself must not re-trigger these gates, hence the ADVANCED_WIRELESS_CONTENT
+	// exemption stays. reaper_fbdone is the operator escape hatch (see httpd.c).
+	else if(`<% nvram_get("reaper_fbdone"); %>` != '1'
+	        && `<% nvram_get("w_Setting"); %>` == '0' && !isSwMode("RP")
+	        && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("QIS_") < 0
+	        && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("ADVANCED_WIRELESS_CONTENT") < 0
+	        && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("REAPER_FIRSTBOOT") < 0)
+		top.location.href = '/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp';
 	else if(isSupport("sdn_mwl") && (isSwMode("RT") || isSwMode("AP"))){
 		const sdn_rl = `<% nvram_get("sdn_rl"); %>`;
 		const sdn_rl_default = `<% nvram_default_get("sdn_rl"); %>`;
-		// Wi-Fi still at factory default -> force the (proven) wireless page until the
-		// user saves a Wi-Fi password; exempt that page itself so they can set it.
-		if(sdn_rl === sdn_rl_default && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("ADVANCED_WIRELESS_CONTENT") < 0)
-			top.location.href = '/Advanced_Wireless_Content.asp?firstboot=1';
+		// Wi-Fi still at factory default -> hand back to the wizard, which owns step 2.
+		if(sdn_rl === sdn_rl_default && `<% nvram_get("reaper_fbdone"); %>` != '1'
+		   && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("ADVANCED_WIRELESS_CONTENT") < 0
+		   && window.location.pathname.toUpperCase().search("REAPER_FIRSTBOOT") < 0)
+			top.location.href = '/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp';
 	}
 }
 
